    "text": "Excalibur stands as the most famous sword in European history. It belonged to King Arthur of Camelot. The Lady of the Lake gave the sword to him. People often confuse it with the rock. The unnamed sword was embedded in rock by the magician Merlin. A prophecy said the man who drew it would become Britain's king. Young Arthur drew it out as if it sank in butter. He broke that sword in battle. Arthur then received Excalibur, forged by the magical smith Wayland. Its scabbard shielded its owner from every wound. Koch showed that name Caladbolg and Caledfwlch. Excalibur is the corrupted medieval form of that old Welsh name.",
